        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Wireless Standards - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "802.11ax / WiFi 6/6E:\n  OFDMA: divide each channel into multiple resource units (RUs)\n    → 9 to 74 simultaneous users per channel (vs. 1 at a time in earlier WiFi)\n    → Key for dense environments (stadium, apartment building)\n  Target Wake Time (TWT): IoT devices agree on wake schedule → battery savings\n  BSS Coloring: spatial reuse by color-coding Basic Service Sets → fewer defer transmissions\n  UL MU-MIMO: 8 clients can transmit simultaneously (vs DL-only in ac)"
    },
    {
