        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Wireless Standards - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BLUETOOTH LOW ENERGY (BLE / Bluetooth 4.0+):\n  Frequency: 2.402-2.480 GHz, 40 channels, 2 MHz spacing\n  Advertising channels: 3 (ch 37, 38, 39) → announce presence\n  Data channels: 37 channels for connected data\n  PHY options:\n    LE 1M: 1 Mbps (original BLE)\n    LE 2M: 2 Mbps (Bluetooth 5)\n    LE Coded (125k / 500k bps): long range, up to 4× range (Bluetooth 5)\n  Tx power: 0.01–100 mW, typical 1 mW\n  Current in deep sleep: µA range → years on coin cell battery"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-WIRELESS-STANDARDS.md#022",
      "path": [
        "08-WIRELESS-STANDARDS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
