        "section": "telecommunications",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Wireless Standards - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MATTER (formerly CHIP — 2022):\n  Application-layer protocol, not a radio protocol\n  Runs over: WiFi, Thread (802.15.4 based), Ethernet\n  Backed by: Apple, Google, Amazon, Samsung, chip vendors\n  Goal: unified smart home standard across ecosystems\n  Apple HomeKit, Google Home, Amazon Alexa — all Matter-compatible\n  Thread: low-power IPv6 mesh (similar to Zigbee PHY but IP stack)\n```"
    },
